nce of about -0.095 versus feature_065=0, meaning stronger dependency, with a 95% interval of roughly -0.167 to -0.024. The estimate is clearly above the approximate 10% threshold, although the least extreme confidence-boundary value is near the threshold. Because this is one of twelve unadjusted discovery tests, I do not accept the opposite claim yet, but the association is promising enough to request independent validation of H7's comparison. I also registered a refinement with direction -1 so that, if validation is favorable, the scientifically meaningful association can be assessed as an opposite-direction claim rather than misrepresenting the original positive hypothesis. I did not validate H4 yet because its interval crosses zero and its exposed group is only moderately sized, despite the large point estimate; validation capacity should focus first on H7. The cell sizes are all valid under the analysis rule, but small or restricted subgroups remain vulnerable to random noise and unmeasured confounding. These are associations in this supplied dataset only, not causal claims or claims about generalizability.",
